// Venus's visuals (read by crates/game; physical data is in body.ron).
// base_color: the cloud top's colour (cloud_top below, sRGB); albedo: Bond albedo, NASA Planetary Fact Sheet (NSSDCA).
(
    base_color: (1.0, 0.99, 0.97),
    albedo: 0.76,
    roughness: 0.95,
    icon_color: (1.00, 0.98, 0.83),
    // The surface (agent SKY; docs/features/solar-visuals.md#venus-and-titan-surfaces): zones from the Magellan
    // C3-MDIR radar mosaic (USGS, 2025 m), k-means centres of its grey levels. Radar brightness is roughness,
    // not colour, so the map does not tint (0) and the zones differ only slightly: Venera 13's colour images,
    // corrected for the orange light, show a dark surface without significant colour (Pieters et al. 1986,
    // Science 234, 1379); reflectance ~0.07 (representative of Venera 13/14's 0.05-0.1).
    color_map: Some("color.jpg"),
    zones: Some((
        map: "zones.png",
        tint: 0.0,
        list: [
            (name: "radar-dark plains", source: (108, 108, 108), albedo: Some((0.065, 0.065, 0.064)),
                pattern: (scale_m: 2000.0, contrast: 0.1)),
            (name: "lava plains", source: (129, 129, 129), albedo: Some((0.070, 0.070, 0.068)),
                pattern: (scale_m: 1500.0, contrast: 0.1)),
            (name: "rough terrain (tesserae, flows, ejecta)", source: (158, 158, 158), albedo: Some((0.078, 0.077, 0.075)),
                pattern: (scale_m: 800.0, contrast: 0.15)),
        ],
    )),
    detail: Some((
        scale_m: 25.0,
        strength: 0.55,
        fade_m: None,
        // Basalt (Venera 13/14: dark, platy).
        rock_color: (0.06, 0.06, 0.058),
    )),
    // The sky (D052, Hillaire) at 680, 550, 440 nm; sources: docs/features/solar-visuals.md#venus (agent SKY).
    // - Rayleigh: CO2 cross-sections 4.89, 11.6, 29.2 e-31 m2 (Sneep & Ubachs 2005) x the surface number
    //   density 9.07e26 m-3 (9.21 MPa, 735 K: body.ron); scale height 8.95 km, which puts VIRA's 3.69 kPa
    //   at 70 km (Seiff et al. 1985, Adv. Space Res. 5(11), 3): the CO2 above the clouds, which is all
    //   that shows from outside (15.9 km, RT/Mg at the surface, put 30 times too much there: a blue veil).
    // - The cloud deck: sulfuric-acid droplets from 47 to 70 km (a tent 46 km wide at 57 km), vertical
    //   optical depth 30 (Pioneer Venus LSAR, Ragent & Blamont 1980: 25-40), asymmetry 0.75 (r_eff 1.05 um,
    //   n 1.44: Hansen & Hovenier 1974); single-scattering albedo 0.9979, 0.9973, 0.9967, from the albedo
    //   of a deep layer, A = 1 - 4 sqrt((1 - w) / (3 (1 - g))), matched to the Bond albedo 0.76 coloured
    //   by the geometric albedos 0.712, 0.689, 0.664 (Mallama et al. 2017): A = 0.786, 0.761, 0.733.
    atmosphere: Some((
        thickness_m: 120000.0,
        rayleigh_scattering: (4.44e-4, 1.056e-3, 2.65e-3),
        rayleigh_scale_height_m: 8950.0,
        mie_scattering: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
        mie_absorption: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
        mie_scale_height_m: 10000.0,
        mie_asymmetry: 0.75,
        layers: [
            (
                scattering: (1.3015e-3, 1.3008e-3, 1.3000e-3),
                absorption: (2.80e-6, 3.50e-6, 4.37e-6),
                asymmetry: (0.75, 0.75, 0.75),
                profile: Tent(center_m: 57000.0, width_m: 46000.0),
            ),
        ],
        // Basaltic plains, dark (Venera 13/14 reflectance ~0.05-0.1).
        ground_albedo: (0.10, 0.07, 0.05),
        // Raymarched inside too: the haze broke the aerial-perspective table into coloured rings.
        raymarch_inside: true,
        // The deck seen from above (docs/features/solar-visuals.md#venus): a Lambert sphere at the cloud top,
        // 74 km (unit optical depth: Ignatiev et al. 2009, JGR 114, E00B43, from VMC/VIRTIS at low and
        // middle latitudes; the tent above puts tau = 1 there too). Albedo: the geometric albedos in
        // Johnson R, V, B, 0.708, 0.689, 0.658 (Mallama et al. 2017, Icarus 282, 19, table 7: the blue
        // drop is the clouds' unknown UV absorber, effective to ~600 nm), times 1.5 (a Lambert sphere's
        // albedo for that geometric albedo), scaled to 1 in red: a Lambert surface cannot exceed 1.
        // Venus is brighter than Lambert near full phase and darker at large phases; A = 1 is within
        // ~16 % of its V phase curve from 30 to 90 deg (Mallama et al. 2006, Icarus 182, 10).
        cloud_top: Some((altitude_m: 74000.0, albedo: (1.0, 0.973, 0.929))),
    )),
)
